an data-text=\"Voturia\" data-n=\"95\" data-lemma=\"Voturia\">VOTURIA</span><span data-text=\"Rufi\" data-n=\"105\" data-lemma=\"Rufus\">RUFI</span>ALYPUSSIMBUL<span data-text=\"Mercurio\" data-n=\"125\" data-lemma=\"Mercurius\">MERCURIO</span><span data-text=\"Augusto\" data-n=\"130\" data-lemma=\"Augustus\">AUGUSTO</span></span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span>  <span>Text: CIL</span>  </span>; </li><li><span class=\"line 5\">line.5: <span>Mommsen oper(a) vel oper(is) opinor</span>  </span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2>English translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\"><a href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7077-0703\">Alex Antoniou</a></p>  <p>[By the order of?] Marcus Albus Pollio, son of Marcus, of [tribe] Oufentina, for the work of Gaius Domitius Rufus, son of Gaius, of [tribe] Voturia, ALYPUS SIMBUL. To Mercury Augustus.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>Manganaro suggests 'ex testamento' rather than 'iussu', and notes that the onomastics are Domitianic. SIMBVL is suggested by Mommsen possibly to be a transliteration of συμβολαιογράφος, a suggestion broadly followed by Manganaro.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Mommsen 1883 <a href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/books/CILv10pII1883\" target=\"_blank\">7224</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589</a>  </li><li> Manganaro 1988 50, 69, 72 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001427</a>  </li><li> Kragelund 2008 120 n.15 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001895\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001895</a>  </li></ul>  <ul><li></li></ul>  </div>  <div id=\"handnote\"> Line 1    Interlineation line 